    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`ZigzagCPStrategy.build_metadata` runs on the scheduler/host side for every prefill-CP batch and creates twelve small int32 device tensors with `torch.tensor(..., device=\"cuda\")`. Each of these is a pageable host-to-device copy, and a pageable H2D copy blocks the host until the work already queued on the current stream has finished. When a previous forward is still in flight (e.g. with PP, or overlap scheduling), the host stalls on every CP prefill batch until the GPU drains.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `layers/cp/zigzag.py`: add `_lists_to_device`, which packs all metadata lists into one pinned host buffer (each segment 16-byte aligned), uploads it once with `non_blocking=True`, and returns per-list int32 views. `build_metadata` now uses it instead of twelve separate `torch.tensor(..., device=...)` calls. The pinned host block is not reused before the copy completes: PyTorch's caching host allocator records an event on the copy stream for non-blocking copies.\n- `layers/cp/utils.py`: docstring note on `prepare_cp_forward` that the metadata tensors are uploaded asynchronously.\n- `test/registered/cp/test_cp_strategy_unit.py`: `_assert_metadata_matches` now also checks values, int32 dtype and 16-byte alignment of every device tensor.\n\nNo change to the metadata values or to any attention kernel.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nQwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-FP8, 4x B300, `--tp-size 2 --pp-size 2 --attn-cp-size 2 --ep-size 2 --enable-prefill-cp --cp-strategy zigzag --cuda-graph-backend-prefill=disabled`, GSM8K 5-shot greedy, full test set (1319):\n\n| | GSM8K |\n|---|---|\n| main | 0.9543 |\n| this PR | 0.9536 |\n\n(one-question difference, within noise; 200-example run: 0.955 vs 0.950)\n\nUnit tests: `python -m unittest test.registered.cp.test_cp_strategy_unit` passes (25 tests) on B300.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nHost time of `ZigzagCPStrategy.build_metadata` (cp_size=8, 4 sequences, 44K extend tokens) on B300, measured with and without a long matmul chain queued on the stream:\n\n| | main p50 | this PR p50 |\n|---|---|---|\n| GPU idle | 0.28 ms | 0.149 ms |\n| GPU busy (forward in flight) | 31.2 ms | 0.185 ms |\n\nWith the GPU busy, main blocks the host until the queued work drains; this PR returns immediately.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41162104299](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41162104299)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41162104315](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41162104315)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41162104417](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41162104417)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
